 "title": "A two-point calibration",
 "caption": "The thermometer reads 1.5 °C in melting ice (true 0 °C) and 98 °C in boiling water (true 100 °C). The straight line through those two points converts any reading: 50 °C read is 50.3 °C true.",
 "alt": "Graph of true temperature against reading, a straight line through (1.5, 0) and (98.0, 100), with the reading 50.0 marked at a true value of 50.3.",
