  "Horizontal axis: the thermometer's reading. Vertical axis: the true temperature.",
  "Fixed points: reading 1.5 at 0 °C (melting ice) and reading 98 at 100 °C (boiling water at 1 atm).",
  "Scale factor = 100 / (98 − 1.5) = 1.0363.",
  "A reading of 50 gives T = (50 − 1.5) × 1.0363 = 50.26 ≈ 50.3 °C."
